 {"id":"fabro-7461","title":"revisor: build the workflow-revisor graph on the lab world (ADR-0011 implementation)","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T15:56:29.250Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-02T16:20:30.619Z","description":"CLOSED 2026-09-02 (cycle 2): the revisor workflow exists and is validated end to end. Commits on denkhaus-lab: 3a57e6229 (graph+prompts+hook), 940e448f8 (review fixes), synced to meta bf54377f3.\n\nBuilt: select (fabro_runs_list, oldest-unrevised-terminal, one per pass, fs_write=\"\") -> analyze (fabro_ask with improve.md question verbatim, review artifact in manual shape, fs_write=.fabro/reviews/**) -> file (sd create, marker report .fabro/revisions/<run-id>.md, shell commit of exact artifact paths, fs_write=.fabro/revisions/**) -> approve (hexagon, fail-closed, Approved LOOPS to select per fork 2, Rejected deadlocks branch, Unanswered soft). Pinned read windows (e47c), least-privilege fabro_tools, stage-journal hook.\n\nVerified: fabro validate OK (info notes only); gate green on both worlds; two-axis review (spec found the missing loop — fixed; standards found fs/prompt convention gaps — fixed). SMOKE RUN 01M1HEGHC7R4FXZ6VERXPB1YJV (succeeded, $0.044, 53s): select picked the oldest terminal run 01M0N5AVYXR7K8PPMGCQRZF90X via real fabro_runs_list (22.6KB result); analyze's fabro_ask FAILED on SandboxUnavailable — the Aug-22 target run's sandbox is pruned; the soft-exit path caught it exactly as designed; journal merged back (29ce54801).\n\nOPEN FORK (user decision pending): the backlog's ancient runs have no sandboxes, so oldest-first livelocks on the first pick. Options: (a) newest-first selection until the engine seeds land, (b) engine fix fabro-HEGG (provision fresh analyst sandbox on reconnect failure), (c) degraded marker path. Filed fabro-HEGG engine seed + selection-order is a one-line prompt change after the fork decision."}
 {"id":"fabro-8d30","title":"engine: live sandbox-availability probe for fabro_runs_list (part a) + fresh analyst sandbox provisioning (part b)","status":"open","type":"bug","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T16:20:30.756Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-02T17:56:23.687Z","description":"PART A DONE 2026-09-02 (commit 128571de7, deployed, PROVEN by revisor run 01M1HKRE686W833SE86D8WD319 which selected a sandbox-alive target and completed analyze->file->gate): live sandbox-availability as a HARD precondition for revisor target selection.\n\nWhy: run containers are stopped at terminal (by design, b5bd restarts them per ask turn) but REMOVED by any prune pass (fabro system prune default >24h, docker container prune, Docker Desktop cleanup) — nothing guarantees retention. The recorded run summary says kind:\"ready\" forever (stale recording, not a live fact), and fabro_runs_list carries no sandbox info at all, so the revisor cannot know before selecting.\n\nDesign:\n- fabro-tool: FabroToolBackend gains ONE probe method (Option<HashSet<RunId>> — None = provider cannot probe); RunSummaryResult gains sandbox_available: Option<bool> (true = container exists, stopped counts; false = removed; null = unknown provider); runs_list calls the probe once per invocation and annotates by set membership.\n- ClientBackend takes an optional Arc<dyn RunSandboxProbe> seam (dependency direction stays server->tool; fabro-tool never depends on docker).\n- fabro-server: DockerRunSandboxProbe — one `docker ps -a --filter label=<managed run label>` call -> HashSet<RunId>; wired where sessions.rs builds ClientBackend. Probe failure -> None + warn log (fail-closed selection, observation counts blocked runs).\n- Revisor select.md: hard rule — only select a run with sandbox_available==true; unrevised-but-blocked runs counted in the journal observation so the backlog stays visible.\n- Docs: child-runs.mdx tool table notes the field.\n\nPART B (follow-up cycle, fabro-8d30 remainder): provision a fresh analyst sandbox (from the run's checkpoint/branch) when reconnect fails because the sandbox is gone — turns blocked backlog entries revisable again.\n\nREMAINING = PART B ONLY: provision a fresh analyst sandbox (from the run's checkpoint/branch) when reconnect fails because the sandbox is gone — turns the blocked backlog entries (~25 runs) revisable again. Part a's probe + hard filter already keep the revisor safe without it."}
